 ## Background
-DynaVol was presented at ICLR 2024 [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the challenge of unsupervised learning of object-centric representations in dynamic visual scenes [S1, unofficial]. Unlike previous approaches that decompose 2D images, DynaVol introduces a 3D scene generative model that unifies geometric structures and object-centric learning [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the principles of dynamic and articulated scene modeling by mapping 3D query points to a canonical space [18219-dynamic-and-articulated-scene-modeling.md].
+DynaVol was presented at ICLR 2024 [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the challenge of unsupervised learning of object-centric representations in dynamic visual scenes [S1, unofficial]. Unlike previous approaches that decompose 2D images, DynaVol introduces a 3D scene generative model that unifies geometric structures and object-centric learning [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the principles of dynamic and articulated scene modeling by mapping 3D query points to a canonical space [G].
 
